### ==========================================
### CUSTOMER SERVICE - REST API 
### ==========================================

### 1. Register Customer
POST http://localhost:8080/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Aina Rahman",
  "email": "aina.test@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0123456789",
  "password": "Test1234",
  "dateOfBirth": "2005-05-15",
  "address": {
    "unitOrHouseNumber": "12A",
    "street": "Jalan Example",
    "city": "Shah Alam",
    "state": "Selangor",
    "postcode": "40150",
    "country": "Malaysia"
  }
}


### 2. Get All Customers
GET http://localhost:8080/customers


### 3. Get Customer by Customer Code
### Replace CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX with the code returned from registration
GET http://localhost:8080/customers/CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX


### 4. Update Customer
### Replace CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX with the registered customer's code
PUT http://localhost:8080/customers/CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Aina Rahman Updated",
  "email": "aina.updated@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0123456789",
  "dateOfBirth": "2005-05-15",
  "address": {
    "unitOrHouseNumber": "20B",
    "street": "Jalan Updated",
    "city": "Shah Alam",
    "state": "Selangor",
    "postcode": "40150",
    "country": "Malaysia"
  }
}


### 5. Get Updated Customer
### Replace CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX with the registered customer's code
GET http://localhost:8080/customers/CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX


### 6. Delete Customer
### Soft delete - record remains in database
### Replace CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX with the registered customer's code
DELETE http://localhost:8080/customers/CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX


### 7. Verify Soft Delete
### Customer should still exist with accountStatus = DELETED
GET http://localhost:8080/customers/CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX


### 8. Non-Existing Customer
GET http://localhost:8080/customers/CUS999999999999


